  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - On 16/05/2025, the proposed use of a room within the dwellinghouse as an office in relation to the private vehicle hire business would be ancillary to the property's use as a single-family dwellinghouse, and would be lawful within the meaning of Sections 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe private vehicle hire business within the property would not have public access, and there would be only one operator at the premises. No external alterations are proposed.  There would be no picking up or dropping off of customers at the site, nor would there be the comings and goings of drivers to the premises.  The nature and scale of the business use would not constitute a material change of use of part or the whole of the house, and therefore, planning permission is not required.\r\n"
